# Builders Bootcamp Page Redesign Plan

The goal is to transform the `builders-bootcamp` subfolder page into a clearer, more premium event one-pager. The current layout is cluttered, and the call-to-actions (CTAs) are not prominent enough. We will align the design with the main page while ensuring the hero section captures all essential information without scrolling.

## Proposed Changes

### [Component Name] Builders Bootcamp Page

#### [MODIFY] [page.tsx](file:///Users/Office/Repos/Clients/JC%20Citadel/jpv-bootcamp/src/app/builders-bootcamp/page.tsx)

- **Hero Section (100vh)**:
    - Implement a full-viewport hero section (`h-screen`).
    - Use a flex or grid layout to center the content.
    - Display key information clearly: **Title**, **Date**, **Time**, **Venue**, and **Primary CTA (Register)**.
    - Use a background treatment (like a subtle gradient or blurred image) to make text pop.
    - Include the event poster in a more integrated way, possibly as a secondary visual or a high-quality preview.
- **Header & Footer**:
    - Ensure they are consistent with the main page ([src/app/page.tsx](file:///Users/Office/Repos/Clients/JC%20Citadel/jpv-bootcamp/src/app/page.tsx)).
    - Keep the "Main site" link in the header.
- **De-cluttering & Spacing**:
    - Increase vertical spacing between sections (e.g., `py-32` instead of `py-24`).
    - Use cleaner card designs for highlights and lists.
    - Group related information better to reduce visual noise.
- **Images**:
    - Use broader, more professional-looking image layouts.
    - Ensure proper aspect ratios and framing.
- **CTAs**:
    - Make "Register now" and "Exhibit" buttons more distinct and prominent.
    - Ensure they are easily accessible and don't get lost in lists.

## Verification Plan

### Manual Verification
- View the page in the browser (if available or via screenshot/recording tools if they show enough).
- Verify the hero section is exactly `100vh` and looks good on desktop/mobile.
- Confirm all links (tickets, exhibits, downloads) work correctly.
- Check that the "Main site" link goes back to the home page.
- Evaluate the overall "cleanliness" and "wow factor" of the design.
